AUDITED ADOPTIONS from levkropp/lccc Aug 19-21 (guilty-until-proven-
innocent; 26 shared functions verified byte-identical, 3 divergent
reviewed line-by-line, 21 lev-only passes audited individually):
- forward_fp_slot_loads (aadab341): FP spill-slot store-to-load
  forwarding with sp-derived base tracking.
- fuse_fp_adjacent_pairs (de451e57): adjacent F64 ldr/str -> ldp/stp,
  4-instruction window with partner-mention/dest-write/base-write
  hazard checks.
- eliminate_repeated_slot_loads + slot-pointer offset folds (b712c79c).
- eliminate_overwritten_moves (339cdb8b): movk correctly excluded from
  MoveWide overwrite kinds.
- fold_zext_move_chains (89111a1f) -- WITH SOUNDNESS FIX, see below.
- eliminate_redundant_sxtb (8a052b9a part 2).
- eliminate_overwritten_stores + sink_loop_carried_stores (69bbce24):
  store sinking restricted to call-free, single-exit, label-free
  bottom-tested regions with the stored register surviving to the
  backedge.
- CCC_NO_REUSE_STACK_LOADS gate + per-pass gates (CCC_NO_FP_PAIR,
  CCC_NO_SLOT_LOAD_DEDUP, CCC_NO_FP_SLOT_FWD, CCC_NO_STORE_DSE,
  CCC_NO_STORE_SINK, CCC_NO_GDSE) for bisection.

REJECTED: his global_dead_store_elimination escape-analysis rewrite
(e20cdf6e/e03da2f1) -- 9 regressions on our tree (volatile_loop,
fp_cmp_inf, unroll_const4_*, gvn_param_alloca_load, hash_narrow_chain,
reduction_two_sums, glibc_ld_builtins; all bisected via CCC_NO_GDSE).
Kept our conservative bail-on-address-of-sp version; REJECTED-ADOPTION
note documents the evidence. His 3 GDSE tests rewritten to the
conservative semantics; 27 of his other peephole tests adopted as-is.

SOUNDNESS FIX in adopted fold_zext_move_chains: his scan treated block
boundaries as proof of death. ret reads x0/x1 (return value!), calls
read x0-x8, branch targets are invisible to a single-block scan. His
version folded d2hi()'s return-value chain into a dead callee-saved
register: 40/100 aarch64_fuzz mismatches at -O1. Now ABI-precise:
ret => live iff x0/x1/x8; call => live iff x0-x8, dead iff x9-x18
(clobbered unread), keep scanning past for x19+; labels/branches =>
live. New test: test_zext_move_chain_blocked_by_ret.

PRE-EXISTING MISCOMPILES found by the adoption battery, both fixed:
1. vectorize insert_remainder_loop derived the scalar-remainder start
   index with the AVX2 byte-offset formula (IV>>3) for the two-wide
   hoisted FmaF64x2 scheme, whose IV is a 4-double GROUP index
   (correct: IV*4). The remainder restarted at element 0 and re-ran the
   whole row: AArch64 matmul at -O2 returned exactly 2x the correct
   value. x86 masked it because its FmaF64x2Hoisted emitter was an
   empty stub (the broken remainder then redid ALL work scalar) -- the
   stub is now a real 4-lane vfmadd231pd implementation using
   regalloc-assigned pointers (same value-cache conflation hazard as
   FmaF64x2). Test: vectorize_axpy_remainder_start.c (x86 + ARM).
2. Default emit_fused_mul_add (traits.rs) loaded  into the
   accumulator FIRST, clobbering the home-less multiply result whose
   only location IS the accumulator (use_count 1: no register, no
   slot). i686's staging fallback then materialised 0:
   returned 1 at -m32 on ALL opt levels (matmul B-matrix init wrote
   identical values everywhere). Add is commutative -- consume the mul
   result as the accumulator-side operand. Test:
   i686_fused_mul_add_operand_order.c (-m32 -O0).

