AUDITED PORT of levkropp e3b21b8f (float Mul;Sub -> fused multiply-
subtract), rewritten for our tree rather than cherry-picked -- our
detect_mul_add_fusions has diverged (window scan over Copy/Cast,
claimed-adds set, FxHashMap fusion map vs his adjacent-only scan):

- detect_mul_add_fusions gains fuse_float_sub: Option<&FxHashSet<u32>>.
  None = backend lacks the instruction or CCC_NO_FMSUB; Some(accs) =
  fuse float Subs except accumulator destinations. Fusing acc -= a*b
  puts the multiply on the loop-carried serial chain (fmsub latency >
  fsub), his measured 13% nbody regression. Verified here: nbody -O2
  assembly is byte-identical with the gate on vs CCC_NO_FMSUB=1;
  mandelbrot gets its expected fmsub.
- Accumulator set = memory-promoted loop F64 phis + surviving Phi dests
  + multi-Copy dests + reverse closure over Copy edges (backedge
  sources sit on the same chain). Ported as a fixpoint over a collected
  edge LIST -- O(rounds*edges), not his O(rounds*whole-function) rescan.
- ARM: fmsub (acc - a*b) / fnmsub (a*b - acc), operand order verified
  against GCC 14 output; all three sources read before the write, so
  output aliasing a source register is safe. x86: vfnmadd231sd/ss
  (acc - product) / vfmsub231sd/ss (product - acc) via the generalized
  emit_scalar_fma231_with helper -- reuses the destructive-coalescing
  and memory-source paths of the shipped fmadd emitter unchanged.
- supports_fused_float_mul_sub gated on fp_contract_fast on both
  backends (same single-rounding contract as fmadd; matches the
  fp-contract matrix: off/default/fast = 0/1/1).
- Trait default for emit_fused_mul_sub is unreachable!() by design: a
  silent mul+sub fallback would hide a backend advertising support
  without implementing the hook, and an emit_int_binop-based fallback
  (levkropp's version) is wrong for floats.
- Rejected from his commit: emitting the integer path through
  emit_int_binop inside the ARM override (dead code -- the detector
  never records integer Subs) and the Sub arm reusing his adjacent-only
  scan (ours supports gap instructions).

PRE-EXISTING BUGS found by the port's differential testing, all
reproduced on upstream main and fixed:

1. x86 scalar FMA emitter skipped the entire instruction when the
   constant multiplier was +0.0 ('if bits != 0' with no else), returning
   acc unchanged. Wrong for x = +/-Inf/NaN (acc + NaN = NaN) and for
   -0.0 + 0.0 = +0.0. Now materializes +0.0 via vxorpd/vxorps and
   fuses. Test: fma_zero_multiplier_semantics.c (lccc now matches gcc:
   '0 -nan ...' not '-0 2 ...').
2. Call staging-hazard pre-spill (session 25) moves rsp by hazard_area
   but did not adjust rsp_frame_size, so every rsp-relative slot read
   emitted while staging the REMAINING arguments read hazard_area bytes
   below its slot. printf with 4 FP args (one freshly computed = hazard,
   three slot-resident) printed stale/garbage args 1-3 at -O1/-O2.
   Fixed by bracketing the staging loop with rsp_frame_size +=/-=
   hazard_area under rsp addressing. Test:
   call_hazard_prespill_rsp_offsets.c.
3. i686 emit_cond_branch_blocks bounced register-homed conditions
   through %eax ('movl %reg,%eax; testl %eax,%eax'), defeating the
   load->widen-cast coalescing on every register-allocated loop
   condition. Now tests the home register in place (testl %reg,%reg;
   read-only, no cache invalidation needed). Un-fails the pre-existing
   check_load_widen_cast_no_relay and validated at runtime (find_c
   returns 'world').

New tests: fmsub_fnmsub_contract.c (x86 + ARM, -ffp-contract=fast,
values exact in binary64 so the test is contract-setting-independent),
